{"units": [{"id": "polys-word80", "translation": "Death, the greatest deliverance from"}, {"id": "polys-word81", "translation": "Now rarely are two cases of this adjective put in one sentence"}, {"id": "polys-word82", "translation": "He accomplished a long journey with much"}, {"id": "polys-word83", "translation": "And I campaigned much with much"}, {"id": "polys-word84", "translation": "Many from many"}, {"id": "polys-word85", "translation": "To fall as oracles to many gods"}, {"id": "polys-word86", "translation": "Slaying many, warming many things in his heart"}, {"id": "polys-word87", "translation": "much"}, {"id": "polys-word88", "translation": "and"}, {"id": "polys-word89", "translation": "So that Darius's great and noble"}, {"id": "polys-word90", "translation": "Many wrestling-bouts and"}, {"id": "polys-word91", "translation": "You look upon many things and, out of the way, well"}, {"id": "polys-word92", "translation": "Many and grievous, unprofitable to me"}, {"id": "polys-word93", "translation": "and"}, {"id": "polys-word94", "translation": "I seem to have suffered much and in vain"}, {"id": "polys-word95", "translation": "She who has suffered much and in vain"}, {"id": "polys-word96", "translation": "And many"}, {"id": "polys-word97", "translation": "For many things—both unfortunate"}, {"id": "polys-word98", "translation": "much"}, {"id": "polys-word99", "translation": "And much"}, {"id": "polys-word100", "translation": "Do not fear; I am winning"}, {"id": "polys-word101", "translation": "much"}, {"id": "polys-word102", "translation": "by much"}, {"id": "polys-word103", "translation": "much of this calamity"}, {"id": "polys-word104", "translation": "I pity these things more than those"}, {"id": "polys-word105", "translation": "much more prudent"}, {"id": "polys-word106", "translation": "most distinguished of the present"}, {"id": "polys-word107", "translation": "by much indeed"}, {"id": "polys-word108", "translation": "many things"}, {"id": "polys-word109", "translation": "O many"}, {"id": "polys-word110", "translation": "He speaks many things against Polynices"}, {"id": "polys-word111", "translation": "For many things from their hands with stones"}, {"id": "polys-word112", "translation": "But when, after many invocations of the gods"}, {"id": "polys-word113", "translation": "Many things at least touch toward"}, {"id": "polys-word114", "translation": "How many things from a dim mind"}, {"id": "polys-word115", "translation": "And to bid many farewells to misfortunes"}, {"id": "polys-word116", "translation": "And many"}, {"id": "polys-word117", "translation": "O wretched in many things, and many"}, {"id": "polys-word118", "translation": "But also to reap these many things"}, {"id": "polys-word119", "translation": "I know that Orestes many things you"}, {"id": "polys-word120", "translation": "And crying aloud"}, {"id": "polys-word121", "translation": "And many things I think"}, {"id": "polys-word122", "translation": "With whom you, often slumbering, at the same time"}, {"id": "polys-word123", "translation": "much"}, {"id": "polys-word124", "translation": "Eteocles alone would be as many throughout the city"}, {"id": "polys-word125", "translation": "much in M"}, {"id": "polys-word126", "translation": "one throughout the whole city"}, {"id": "polys-word127", "translation": "And much of the sea"}, {"id": "polys-word128", "translation": "A thick cloak from above, threefold"}, {"id": "polys-word129", "translation": "Many nooses from above for my neck"}, {"id": "polys-word130", "translation": "The form πολλός, which Sophocles and Euripides use elsewhere, for example"}, {"id": "polys-word131", "translation": "In Aeschylus there are none"}, {"id": "polys-word132", "translation": "The form vero poetica πολεῖ for πολλῷ is one example"}, {"id": "polys-word133", "translation": "With dark πολεῖ"}, {"id": "polys-word134", "translation": "And the plural πολέα for πολλά"}, {"id": "polys-word135", "translation": "And many he had in"}, {"id": "polys-word136", "translation": "The many missiles, all mixed, many—Lachmann on account of the verse antistrophic πολύδονα σώμαθ᾽"}, {"id": "polys-word137", "translation": "Which is not appropriate, since the two verses do not correspond accurately to each other"}, {"id": "polys-word138", "translation": "On the comparative πλείων and superlative πλεῖστος we have spoken in their place"}, {"id": "polysines-orth1", "translation": "much-harming"}, {"id": "polysines-def1", "translation": "much-harming"}, {"id": "polysines-note1", "translation": "Μυχοῦ δ᾽ ἄφερκτος πολυσινοῦς κυνὸς [and from the recess, unguarded, of the much-harming dog]"}, {"id": "polysines-note2", "translation": "πολυσίνους [much-harming] M, but with the sigma expunged"}, {"id": "polysines-quote1", "translation": "justice"}, {"id": "polysines-word1", "translation": "and from the recess, unguarded, of the much-harming dog"}, {"id": "polysines-word2", "translation": "much-harming M"}, {"id": "polystephos-orth1", "translation": "much-garlanded"}, {"id": "polystephos-def1", "translation": "crowned with many garlands"}, {"id": "polystephos-note1", "translation": "Ἔρπω πρὸς πολυστεφῆ [I creep toward the much-garlanded]"}, {"id": "polystephos-quote1", "translation": "recess"}, {"id": "polystephos-word1", "translation": "I creep toward the much-garlanded"}, {"id": "polystomeo-orth1", "translation": "to speak much"}, {"id": "polystomeo-def1", "translation": "I am talkative"}, {"id": "polystomeo-note1", "translation": "Καὶ ξυμβολοῦσιν οὐ [and to those who meet, not]"}, {"id": "polystomeo-quote1", "translation": "to speak much"}, {"id": "polystomeo-word1", "translation": "and to those who meet, not"}, {"id": "polystonos-orth1", "translation": "much-groaning"}, {"id": "polystonos-def1", "translation": "causing many groans"}, {"id": "polystonos-note1", "translation": "Ἰὼ πολύστονοι τόδ᾽ [Alas, much-groaning this]"}, {"id": "polystonos-note2", "translation": "Πολύστονος [much-groaning]"}, {"id": "polystonos-note